{"claims":[{"excerpt":"CPython 3.13 Free Threading and Extension Imports","claim":"The piece connects CPython 3.13 free threading with the behavior of extension imports.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0","evidence":"CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading, a configuration that can run with the global interpreter lock disabled. An extension must explicitly indicate that it supports this mode; importing one without that declaration warns and enables the GIL.","narrative":"Explain how CPython 3.13’s experimental free-threading configuration connects an application’s runtime choice to what happens when it imports an extension.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The title accurately identifies the topics and relationship developed in the piece and supported by the source.","materiality":"Low; it describes the piece’s subject."},{"excerpt":"CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading as a configuration in which the Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) can be disabled.","claim":"CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading as a configuration that can disable the GIL.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading, a configuration that can run with the global interpreter lock disabled.","narrative":"Establish that CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading as a configuration in which the GIL can be disabled.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The piece preserves the source’s version, experimental status, and configuration-level description.","materiality":"Material context for the runtime behavior discussed."},{"excerpt":"What happens next depends in part on the extensions an application imports.","claim":"An application’s imported extensions can affect what happens when it uses the free-threading configuration.","category":"cause","label":"F0","evidence":"An extension must explicitly indicate that it supports this mode; importin