ing support for free threading is a compatibility signal, not a guarantee that an extension is thread-safe.","claim":"Declaring support for free threading signals compatibility but does not guarantee that the extension is thread-safe.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"a support declaration is distinct from the work of making code thread-safe.","narrative":"declaring support for the mode is separate from making the extension’s code thread-safe.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The distinction is explicit in the source and retained in the piece.","materiality":"Material; it prevents readers from treating the declaration as a thread-safety guarantee."},{"excerpt":"Extension authors have a separate responsibility to make the extension’s code thread-safe.","claim":"Extension authors have responsibility for making their extension’s code thread-safe, distinct from declaring support for free threading.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"a support declaration is distinct from the work of making code thread-safe.","narrative":"extension authors have a distinct compatibility responsibility: declaring support for the mode is separate from making the extension’s code thread-safe.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes declaring support from the work of making code thread-safe; the piece expresses that distinction as a separate author responsibility.","materiality":"Material; it clarifies that declaring compatibility alone does not make extension code safe for concurrent execution."}]}

